Dustbunny is an educational project that I am using to learn C.
The use of AI agents/LLMs to do all the coding for me, will not help me learn C.
For that reason I want to make it clear to myself, and to everyone where AI is used in this project.

AI will only be used in large places of repetitive code that would be otherwise tedious and time-wasting to write by hand.
For example, a long switch statement.

If I find an alternative solution where I would not have to write such repetive code, I will use it, and no AI will be involved.

AI will also be used to generate place-holder scripts, like the release.sh script in this repo.

AI was used to explain how to create the contents of packaging/ and repo/, but the contents themselves were created either by hand or using a tool that manages it automatically.

If I encounter a problem in the code that I can not solve myself, I will always lean towards asking real humans rather than an AI.

Anything that has been generated is strictly reviewed and modified to be as suitable as it can be.